**Formula:** $C[i][j] = \sum_{k=0}^{2} A[i][k] \times B[k][j]$ (row $i$ of A times column $j$ of B).

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    int a[3][3], b[3][3], c[3][3], i, j, k;

    printf("Enter elements of matrix A (3x3):\n");
    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
        for (j = 0; j < 3; j++)
            scanf("%d", &a[i][j]);

    printf("Enter elements of matrix B (3x3):\n");
    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
        for (j = 0; j < 3; j++)
            scanf("%d", &b[i][j]);

    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
        for (j = 0; j < 3; j++) {
            c[i][j] = 0;
            for (k = 0; k < 3; k++)
                c[i][j] += a[i][k] * b[k][j];
        }

    printf("Product matrix C = A x B:\n");
    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
        for (j = 0; j < 3; j++)
            printf("%d\t", c[i][j]);
        printf("\n");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

**Sample run:** A = `1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9`, B = identity `1 0 0 / 0 1 0 / 0 0 1` gives C = A. With A = B = `1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9`, C = `30 36 42 / 66 81 96 / 102 126 150`.

**Idea:** multiplication is repeated addition:
$$a \times b = a + a \times (b-1), \qquad a \times 0 = 0$$
If b is negative, compute $a \times |b|$ and change the sign.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int multiply(int a, int b)
{
    if (b == 0)                     /* base case */
        return 0;
    if (b < 0)                      /* handle negative multiplier */
        return -multiply(a, -b);
    return a + multiply(a, b - 1);  /* a added b times */
}

int main()
{
    int a, b;
    printf("Enter two numbers: ");
    scanf("%d %d", &a, &b);
    printf("\n%d x %d = %d\n", a, b, multiply(a, b));
    return 0;
}
```

**Trace for 6 x 4:** 6 + multiply(6,3) = 6 + 6 + multiply(6,2) = 6 + 6 + 6 + multiply(6,1) = 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + 0 = 24.

