**Logic**
- A number `m > 1` is prime if no `i` from 2 to $\sqrt{m}$ divides it.
- Choice `p`/`P`: start at `Num - 1` and move **down** until a prime is found (the largest prime less than Num).
- Choice `N` (also `n`): start at `Num + 1` and move **up** until a prime is found (the smallest prime greater than Num).
- Since Num > 10, a prime below Num always exists (e.g. 7), and a prime above any number always exists.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int isPrime(int m)
{
    int i;
    if (m < 2) return 0;
    for (i = 2; i * i <= m; i++)
        if (m % i == 0)
            return 0;
    return 1;
}

int main(void)
{
    int Num, M;
    char Choice;

    printf("Enter Num (> 10): ");
    scanf("%d", &Num);
    printf("Enter Choice (P/N): ");
    scanf(" %c", &Choice);          /* space skips the leftover newline */

    if (Num <= 10)
    {
        printf("Num must be greater than 10\n");
        return 1;
    }

    if (Choice == 'p' || Choice == 'P')
    {
        M = Num - 1;
        while (!isPrime(M))
            M--;
        printf("Prime number less than %d: %d\n", Num, M);
    }
    else if (Choice == 'N' || Choice == 'n')
    {
        M = Num + 1;
        while (!isPrime(M))
            M++;
        printf("Prime number greater than %d: %d\n", Num, M);
    }
    else
        printf("Invalid choice\n");

    return 0;
}
```

**Sample runs**

| Num | Choice | Output |
|---|---|---|
| 20 | P | `Prime number less than 20: 19` |
| 20 | N | `Prime number greater than 20: 23` |
| 24 | p | `Prime number less than 24: 23` |

