$$\max = \frac{a + b + |a - b|}{2}, \qquad \min = \frac{a + b - |a - b|}{2}$$

Proof: if $a \ge b$, $|a-b| = a-b$, so max $= \frac{2a}{2} = a$, min $= \frac{2b}{2} = b$. If $a < b$, $|a-b| = b-a$, so max $= b$, min $= a$.

