**Method 2: using bitwise XOR** (no overflow risk)

```c
a = a ^ b;
b = a ^ b;   /* (a^b)^b = a */
a = a ^ b;   /* (a^b)^a = b */
```

Both swap the values without a third variable. (Method 1 can overflow for very large values; XOR fails if `a` and `b` are the same variable, e.g. via pointers.)

