**Mathematics:**
- (i) Sum of the first N odd numbers: $1 + 3 + \dots + (2N-1) = N^2$. N = 4 gives 16.
- (ii) Odd numbers from the (M+1)-th to the P-th (there are P - M of them), e.g. M = 4, P = 6: 9 + 11 = 20. This equals
$$\text{sum} = P^2 - M^2 = 36 - 16 = 20$$

**No `+` or `-`:** multiplication is allowed, and the subtraction $P^2 - M^2$ is done with bitwise operators: `a ^ b` gives the difference bits, `(~a) & b` gives the borrows, which are shifted left and applied again until there is no borrow.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int subtract(int a, int b)        /* a - b using only bitwise operators */
{
    int borrow;
    while (b != 0) {
        borrow = (~a) & b;
        a = a ^ b;
        b = borrow << 1;
    }
    return a;
}

int main()
{
    int n, m, p;
    printf("Enter N: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);
    printf("Enter M and P (M < P): ");
    scanf("%d %d", &m, &p);
    printf("\n(i)  Sum of first %d odd numbers = %d\n", n, n * n);
    printf("(ii) Sum of %d odd numbers after the first %d = %d\n",
           subtract(p, m), m, subtract(p * p, m * m));
    return 0;
}
```

**Cross check** (N = 4, M = 4, P = 6):
```
Enter N: Enter M and P (M < P): 
(i)  Sum of first 4 odd numbers = 16
(ii) Sum of 2 odd numbers after the first 4 = 20
```

**Method:** compare the last digits of the number and of its square one by one. If every digit of n matches the corresponding last digit of $n^2$, the number is automorphic.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    long long n, sq, t;
    int automorphic = 1;
    printf("Enter a number: ");
    scanf("%lld", &n);
    sq = n * n;
    t = n;
    while (t > 0) {
        if (t % 10 != sq % 10) {    /* a digit does not match */
            automorphic = 0;
            break;
        }
        t = t / 10;
        sq = sq / 10;
    }
    if (automorphic)
        printf("\n%lld is an Automorphic number\n", n);
    else
        printf("\n%lld is not an Automorphic number\n", n);
    return 0;
}
```

**Trace for 376:** $376^2 = 141376$. Digits compared: 6 = 6, 7 = 7, 3 = 3, so automorphic.

**Sample run** (input `376`):
