**Analysis (N = 5):** each row has $2N - 1 = 9$ columns. Column j (1 to 9) shows the value $2N - j$ (9 down to 1). In row i (1 to N) the middle $2i - 3$ columns become `*`, i.e. column j is a star when $|j - N| < i - 1$.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int n, i, j, dist;
    printf("Enter number of rows: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);
    printf("\n");
    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (j = 1; j <= 2 * n - 1; j++) {
            dist = j - n;
            if (dist < 0) dist = -dist;         /* distance from centre */
            if (dist < i - 1)
                printf("* ");
            else
                printf("%d ", 2 * n - j);
        }
        printf("\n");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

