**Analysing row i (1 to N):**
- Leading spaces: $2(N-i)$ (each number takes 2 columns).
- Rising part: i, i+1, ..., 2i-1 (i numbers).
- Falling part: 2i-2, 2i-3, ..., i (i-1 numbers).

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
    int n, i, j;
    printf("Enter number of rows: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);
    printf("\n");
    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        for (j = 1; j <= 2 * (n - i); j++)   /* leading spaces */
            printf(" ");
        for (j = i; j <= 2 * i - 1; j++)     /* rising: i .. 2i-1 */
            printf("%d ", j);
        for (j = 2 * i - 2; j >= i; j--)     /* falling: 2i-2 .. i */
            printf("%d ", j);
        printf("\n");
    }
    return 0;
}
