**Finding the rule:** in row `i` and column `j` (both 1 to 5) the entry is $j \cdot i^{j}$.

Check, row 2: $1\cdot2=2,\ 2\cdot4=8,\ 3\cdot8=24,\ 4\cdot16=64,\ 5\cdot32=160$. Row 3: $3, 18, 81, 324, 1215$. Row 5, column 5: $5\cdot5^5 = 15625$. Row 1 gives $1,2,3,4,5$.

So inside row `i` keep `p` = $i^j$ by multiplying by `i` each column, and print `j * p` with `%5d`.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    int i, j;
    long p;

    for (i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
    {
        p = 1;
        for (j = 1; j <= 5; j++)
        {
            p = p * i;                 /* p = i^j */
            printf("%5ld", j * p);     /* right justified, width 5 */
        }
        printf("\n");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

